IVX AUTONOMOUS 24/7 — FINAL 9/10 TO 10/10 EXECUTION MODE

STATUS:
Authentication restored.
GitHub access verified.
Render access verified.
Owner session verified.
PR #16 created.
Production SHA parity verified.

OBJECTIVE:

Operate continuously, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, to complete IVX IA and IVX Autonomous from the current 9/10 state to verified enterprise-grade stability.

Do not wait for repeated owner prompts.
Do not stop after one PR.
Do not stop because one task is blocked.
Do not create new product features until stabilization is complete.

==================================================
1. WORK CONTINUOUSLY
==================================================

Run this loop continuously:

1. Check production health.
2. Check GitHub Actions.
3. Check open PRs.
4. Check active incidents.
5. Check the engineering backlog.
6. Select the highest-priority unblocked issue.
7. Repair it in an isolated branch.
8. Add regression tests.
9. Commit and push.
10. Open or update a PR.
11. Monitor CI.
12. Repair relevant CI failures.
13. Prepare deployment evidence.
14. Request owner approval only when required.
15. Continue immediately with the next safe issue.

A blocked task must not stop unrelated safe engineering work.

==================================================
2. CURRENT TASK — PR #16
==================================================

Complete PR #16:

- monitor CI;
- fix any failure caused by the PR;
- verify TypeScript, lint and relevant tests;
- wait for owner approval if merge approval is required;
- merge only after CI passes;
- deploy through Render;
- capture deployment ID;
- verify /health and /version;
- prove SHA parity;
- record evidence.

After PR #16 is complete, automatically begin the next backlog task.

Do not wait for another owner message.

==================================================
3. EXACT PRIORITY ORDER
==================================================

P0 — SOURCE AND DEPLOYMENT CONTROL

1. Block every direct write to main.
2. Block Git Data API mutation of main.
3. Remove all alternate production branches.
4. Require branch → PR → CI → merge.
5. Require a real Render deployment ID.
6. Prevent false COMPLETED states.
7. Enforce GitHub/CI/Render/runtime SHA parity.
8. Remove hard-coded owner credentials.
9. Verify zero active Rork production dependency.

P0 — CI AND BUILD STABILITY

10. Fix every IVX CI failure.
11. Fix IVX QA Suite.
12. Fix IVX E2E Acceptance Pipeline.
13. Fix Android Emulator QA.
14. Fix iOS Simulator QA.
15. Fix Expo/Gradle version consistency.
16. Fix Android signing separation.
17. Obtain three consecutive successful workflow runs.

P1 — AUTONOMOUS RELIABILITY

18. Fix request attachment and job replacement.
19. Add request idempotency.
20. Preserve CANCELLED status correctly.
21. Revalidate approvals before resume.
22. Make state writes atomic.
23. Expand zombie-job detection.
24. Make durable storage authoritative.
25. Verify restart recovery.
26. Verify rollback.

P1 — IVX IA PRODUCT STABILITY

27. Owner login.
28. Session persistence.
29. Registration.
30. IVX IA chat loading.
31. Message ordering and duplicate prevention.
32. Reels and media.
33. Uploads.
34. Notifications.
35. Android crashes.
36. iOS crashes.
37. API and database reliability.

P2 — QUALITY

38. TypeScript.
39. Lint.
40. Dead code.
41. Duplicate code.
42. Dependency cleanup.
43. Security.
44. Performance.
45. Test coverage.
46. Architecture documentation.
47. Technical debt.

==================================================
4. ONE ISSUE PER BRANCH
==================================================

For every issue:

1. Reproduce the defect.
2. Identify exact file and function.
3. Create:
   auto-fix/<task-id>-<short-name>
4. Add a failing regression test.
5. Confirm it fails before the fix.
6. Apply the smallest safe fix.
7. Run focused tests.
8. Run TypeScript.
9. Run lint.
10. Run relevant integration/E2E tests.
11. Scan changed files for secrets.
12. Review the diff.
13. Commit.
14. Push.
15. Open PR.
16. Monitor CI.
17. Record evidence.

Never combine unrelated defects in one PR.

Never edit main directly.

==================================================
5. AUTHORITY WITHOUT MICROMANAGEMENT
==================================================

Autonomous may perform without repeated owner approval:

- code inspection;
- branch creation;
- safe code changes;
- test creation;
- TypeScript/lint fixes;
- workflow repair;
- CI repair;
- dead-code cleanup;
- duplicate-code cleanup;
- safe internal refactors;
- commits;
- pushes;
- PR creation;
- CI monitoring;
- evidence preparation.

Owner approval is required only for:

- production deployment;
- database migration;
- RLS changes;
- authentication behavior changes;
- payments;
- data deletion;
- secret rotation;
- production signing;
- AWS, DNS, Render or Supabase infrastructure changes;
- destructive architecture changes.

If approval is required:

- mark the task WAITING_OWNER_APPROVAL;
- send one concise notification;
- continue with the next safe independent task.

==================================================
6. TRUTHFUL COMPLETION
==================================================

Never mark a task VERIFIED because a commit exists.

VERIFIED requires:

- job ID;
- branch;
- commit SHA;
- remote SHA;
- PR URL;
- CI run ID;
- test result;
- merge SHA when applicable;
- Render deployment ID when applicable;
- /health HTTP 200;
- /version HTTP 200;
- SHA parity;
- production smoke test;
- timestamp.

If any evidence is missing, use:

- FAILED
- BLOCKED_CREDENTIAL
- BLOCKED_OWNER_APPROVAL
- CODE_COMPLETE_NOT_DEPLOYED
- DEPLOYED_NOT_VERIFIED

==================================================
7. SELF-HEALING
==================================================

Continuously detect:

- crashes;
- HTTP 4xx/5xx spikes;
- CI failures;
- Render failures;
- Supabase failures;
- stuck workers;
- missing heartbeat;
- SHA mismatches;
- duplicate messages;
- blank screens;
- infinite loading;
- failed uploads;
- failed notifications;
- Android/iOS startup failures;
- performance regressions.

For each incident:

detect
→ preserve evidence
→ reproduce
→ create branch
→ add regression test
→ repair
→ test
→ PR
→ CI
→ approval when required
→ deploy
→ verify
→ close incident

Automatically roll back when a newly deployed change causes a critical production failure and rollback is safe.

==================================================
8. REPORTING
==================================================

Post concise reports inside IVX IA Chat:

Every two hours:

- completed tasks;
- active task;
- queued P0/P1 tasks;
- PRs;
- CI run IDs;
- failures;
- GitHub SHA;
- Render SHA;
- runtime SHA;
- incidents;
- rollbacks;
- approvals required;
- next three tasks.

Executive reports:

- 7:00 AM
- 7:00 PM

Immediate alerts only for:

- production outage;
- security incident;
- data-loss risk;
- failed deployment;
- failed rollback;
- critical missing credential;
- owner approval required.

Do not repeat narrative reports.

==================================================
9. FINAL 10/10 ACCEPTANCE
==================================================

Return:

IVX_10_10_AUTONOMOUS_VERIFIED

only when:

- all P0 gaps are closed;
- all required workflows pass three consecutive times;
- main is the only production source;
- no direct main-write path exists;
- deployment evidence is complete;
- SHA parity is enforced;
- no false COMPLETED states exist;
- restart recovery passes;
- rollback passes;
- self-healing proofs pass;
- Android/iOS critical QA passes;
- owner controls all credentials and infrastructure;
- zero active Rork runtime dependency exists;
- the engineering backlog is empty or contains only approved future improvements.

Until then, continue working 24/7.

START NOW BY COMPLETING PR #16.
THEN CONTINUE AUTOMATICALLY THROUGH THE BACKLOG.
DO NOT WAIT FOR ADDITIONAL OWNER INSTRUCTIONS.
